# No scrape runs without being told

Do not start a `scrape-*` recipe, the ingest modules behind them, an
experiment script, or any other job that calls an LLM or runs for minutes,
unless the user asked for that specific run in this conversation.

- Permission for one run does not carry over to the next, even on an isolated
  schema, even at the same cost.
- "Checking that my change works" is not a reason. `pytest -m "not llm"` is
  the verification the agent may run unasked; anything past that is stated as
  unverified, with the command offered for the user to run.
- When a run seems worth doing, say so in one line with the expected duration
  and cost, and wait for a yes.

Context: an eight-minute, ~120-call ingest was launched as a "smoke run" after
the user had authorised only an earlier experiment.
